-- title:
--   Roof prolongation at level Nℓ over a level-N reduction datum
-- statement:
--   Fix $N$ with $N\neq 0$, a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N$, a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (so $A$ lies over $q$), and a prime $\ell\neq q$; write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$. Assume the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $N\ell$ are integral ring homomorphisms, both over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — `heckeAlphaBar`, the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` into `modularFunctionFieldBar (N*ℓ)`, and `heckeBetaBar`, induced by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ on Laurent series — and over $\kappa$: `heckeAlphaC`, the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` into `charLDegeneracyRoof κ N ℓ` (the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by `jqModC`, `jqNModC N`, `jqNModC ℓ`, `jqNModC (N*ℓ)`), and `heckeBetaC`, induced by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$. Assume further that each of these three fields has principal divisors (every nonzero $f$ admits a divisor matching all its orders and of degree $0$), that every place of the roof over $\kappa$ has residue degree $1$, and that a regular prolongation $R_1$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar N` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` is given together with a map $r_1$ on places such that for every $R_1$-integral $f$ with nonzero residue and every divisor $D$ computing the orders of $f$, the image $\mathrm{mapDomain}\,r_1\,D$ computes the orders of $R_1$-residue of $f$; finally, that the base-changed $j$-expansion $jq$ and its $N$-fold $q$-expansion are $R_1$-integral with residues `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ N`. Then there exist a regular prolongation $R_\ell$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar (N*ℓ)` with values in `charLDegeneracyRoof κ N ℓ` and a map $r_\ell$ on places satisfying the same order law, such that for every $R_1$-integral $f$ both `heckeAlphaBar f` and `heckeBetaBar f` are $R_\ell$-integral with residues `heckeAlphaC` resp. `heckeBetaC` applied to the residue of $f$, and such that for every place $v$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` the degree of the pullback of the divisor $(v,1)$ along `heckeAlphaBar` equals the degree of the pullback of $(r_1v,1)$ along `heckeAlphaC`, and likewise for the two $\beta$ maps.
--
--   This is the good-reduction statement for the level-$N\ell$ modular function field at a prime $q$ not dividing $N\ell$, in the form of a prolongation of a valuation ring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with both degeneracy maps and with the reduction of places and divisors; the two generator clauses pin down $R_1$ as the constant-reduction datum and thereby fix $R_\ell$ over it. It feeds the place-specialisation results that match the level-$N$ Hecke correspondence with its reduction and compute the associated divisors on the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_charLDegeneracyRoof_regularProlongation_heckeCompat_of_ne_of_residue_jq_jqN.lean

